# Edge (Cloudflare)

- The Worker enforces capability tokens. It never decides who may upload.
- Stream request bodies to R2. Do not buffer a whole file in memory.
- Durable Object: one per user vault, Hibernation API, SQLite backend (`new_sqlite_classes`).
- R2 keys are server-generated UUIDs. Bucket is private. No public access. No custom domain.
- Downloads: `Content-Disposition: attachment` and `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`. Never render a user blob inline at this origin.
- Cron prunes expired rows, orphaned R2 objects, and uncommitted blobs older than 1 hour.

```ts
// BAD
const buf = await request.arrayBuffer();
await env.BLOBS.put(key, buf);

// GOOD
await env.BLOBS.put(key, request.body, { httpMetadata: { contentType: "application/octet-stream" } });
```
